  "review": {
    "review": "The hero remained alive at 26/80 HP when the planner stopped. The initiating defect was stale door bookkeeping after Tengu's final arena replacement. Door 746 had already been crossed at decisions 4489–4490 (accepted log lines 13133 and 13135). Decision 4586's accepted transition (line 13391) records the defeat and relocation; decision 4587 observes the same door closed and visible. The bot correctly collected the mask in decisions 4587–4588, but decision 4589 reported no unopened doors and exhausted planning (lines 13398–13399). The door retained the same closed terrain value, so the terrain-change refresh missed it, while historical visits excluded it from exploration. The pinned game source confirms final victory replaces this map. A focused correction rearms publicly observed closed doors once on confirmed final victory, retaining normal route, hazard, failed-movement and pickup checks. A reduced evidence-derived fixture, not recovered runtime memory, fails with two expected assertions on original policy and passes all five tests with the correction. No gameplay was replayed. This establishes door admission, not successful exit discovery, descent or survival.",
    "learnings": "A boss victory can replace the map without changing a previously crossed door's terrain value. Treat freshly observed closed doors as new work once after confirmed final Tengu victory, while preserving reward pickup and all existing movement safety checks. Selecting the route is not evidence of crossing it or reaching the exit."
  },
